id=a52sxq_wallpaper_interactive
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Samsung Interactive wallpapers (Galaxy S24 Ultra set, re-encoded for the SM7325 decoder)
author=kusti420
description=Brings back the "Featured" Interactive wallpapers (Wallpaper and style > Featured, Interactive badge) that patches/wallpaper has to strip: they are SpriteWallpaper InfinityWallpaper clips (com.samsung.android.wallpaper.live.infinity.InfinityWallpaper, MediaExtractor + MediaCodec, one seek per Choreographer tick to frame*1000000/fps, so the clip must be all-intra), stored as res/raw/video_00N.mp4 in /system/priv-app/wallpaper-res/wallpaper-res.apk and listed as type 10 / content_type "infinity" entries in res/raw/resources_info.json. The S26U source clips are 1440x3120 HEVC Main10 90 fps (134 MB each), above the c2.qti.hevc.decoder budget (media_codecs_yupik_v1.xml: 16x16 blocks, 1044480 blocks/s, performance point 1920x1080@120), so patches/wallpaper converts those entries to stills; this patch (sorted after it under LC_ALL=C) adds the Galaxy S24 Ultra set instead. Source: SM-S928B EUX S928BXXS6EZJ1 (fetched PC-side with samloader, system partition of super.img, wallpaper-res.apk only; nothing of it is flashed): res/raw/E3_Infinite_Video_Wallpaper_{ZKLG,ZT,ZVLB,ZYZO}.mp4, 1440x3120 HEVC Main10 120 fps all-intra, 2953 frames, 24.6 s, 52-53 Mbit/s, 162-163 MB each, colours black / warm gray / violet / yellow (str_id_black, str_id_warm_gray, str_id_violet, str_id_yellow all exist in our wallpaper-res strings, so desc_str_id is kept). Transcode (ffmpeg, libx265 4.3): fps=30 (every 4th frame), crop 1404x3120 centred (2.167:1 -> 2.222:1), lanczos scale to 1080x2400, yuv420p 8-bit, every frame forced IDR_N_LP (-force_key_frames expr:1 -forced-idr 1, x265 keyint=250 open-gop=0 bframes=0: keyint=1 would make x265 signal the RExt intra profile idc 4, which the decoder does not advertise, this way the all-intra stream is signalled Main idc 1 like Samsung's own Main10 all-intra clips), CRF 21 preset slow, level 5.0, hvc1, no audio; 738 frames per clip, see prebuilts/wallpapers/s24u/README.txt for the sizes and bitrates. The S24U json (0.0.7) carries no transition_frame_info: the One UI 8 engine used its built-in table, which SpriteWallpaper 2.8.78 still has (infinity/c.<clinit>, SEM_FIRST_SDK_INT < 35 branch: "AOD AOD 0 300 1200 / AOD LOCK 0 720 1800 / AOD HOME 0 2952 2500 / LOCK HOME 720 2952 1200 / LOCK TOUCH 720 1800 1000", written for these 2953-frame 120 fps clips). Because the clips are re-timed, that table is written explicitly into each entry with every frame number scaled by 30/120 (0 75 / 0 180 / 0 737 / 180 737 / 180 450, clamped to the last frame), the durations unchanged, thumbnails at frame 0 as on the S24U. Decoder budget per transition at 1080x2400 (10125 blocks/frame): AOD AOD 76 frames in 1.2 s = 641k blocks/s and AOD LOCK 181 frames in 1.8 s = 1.018M blocks/s are under the 1.044M cap; the three scrubs (AOD HOME 738 frames in 2.5 s, LOCK HOME 558 in 1.2 s, LOCK TOUCH 271 in 1.0 s) cover more frames than any display can show, and the engine only seeks to one frame per vsync (ValueAnimator frame index), so their decode rate is bounded by the refresh rate: 60 Hz = 608k, 120 Hz = 1.215M blocks/s, 16 percent over the declared cap, within the 1920x1080@120 performance point (1.25x the pixels), and the player never checks CodecCapabilities, so the worst case is a late frame during the swipe, never a failed configure. ID reuse: no resources.arsc edit, the clips take over raw/video_001..video_004 (0x7f020005..0x7f020008; video_005/006 stay empty and unreferenced); the entries are deep copies of the S26U type-10 entries (schema of the 2.8.78 parser: which=7, target_screen_only, type_params, cmf_info, logging_info) with isDefault=false so the default wallpaper stays the still image. The APK is re-signed with the platform key exactly like patches/wallpaper (signapk, aosp or unica platform cert).
